// Title: Use of VSIISExeLauncher.exe
// Sigma ID: 18749301-f1c5-4efc-a4c3-276ff1f5b6f8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: The "VSIISExeLauncher.exe" binary part of the Visual Studio/VS Code can be used to execute
//   arbitrary binaries
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/VSIISExeLauncher/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_vsiisexelauncher.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\VSIISExeLauncher.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "VSIISExeLauncher.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -p " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -a ")
